COLLECE

"For the strength of the hills, we bless thee,

Our God, our fathers'God;

Thou hast made thy children mighty,

By the touch of the mountain sod."

Not for the strength of the hills in a mere physical sense, but for their strength in the sense of the rich treasures which they contain, for the rocks and soil which are yearly washed down into the valleys to replenish our already fertile soil. For these, O,

Lord, we bless thee.

"Thou hast made thy children mighty, by the touch of the mountain sod."

Those who till the soil are truly made mighty. There are no

soils in the world deeper or more fertile than the soils that yield so abundantly and readily to the touch of cultivation and irrigation in these mountain valleys.

So the author of the above song said probably more than he knew, when the inspired words came from his pen.

